00:48:13.720 --> 00:48:13.920
Okay.

1214
00:48:14.300 --> 00:48:14.820
All right.

1215
00:48:14.880 --> 00:48:18.500
This is a very sort of dorky actor moment, so just bear with me.

1216
00:48:18.640 --> 00:48:24.700
But I thought John, as Jim, did such a fantastic job on the phone with Mr. Decker when he loses

1217
00:48:24.700 --> 00:48:25.940
his sale to Dwight.

1218
00:48:26.040 --> 00:48:31.120
Oh, it is one of the hardest things in the world to have a fake one-sided phone conversation.

1219
00:48:31.340 --> 00:48:33.100
That has hills and valleys of emotion.

1220
00:48:33.260 --> 00:48:33.400
Yes.

1221
00:48:33.400 --> 00:48:38.120
Or you're reacting, like, he's excited, then he's disappointed, then he, like, figures out

1222
00:48:38.120 --> 00:48:38.760
what happened.

1223
00:48:38.800 --> 00:48:40.640
And there's no one on the other line.

1224
00:48:40.800 --> 00:48:41.400
No one.

1225
00:48:41.640 --> 00:48:42.920
There's no one speaking to you.

1226
00:48:43.040 --> 00:48:44.620
John is just doing that on his own.

1227
00:48:44.780 --> 00:48:44.880
Yes.

1228
00:48:44.880 --> 00:48:46.740
And I just sat there, and I rewatched it.

1229
00:48:46.800 --> 00:48:49.260
And, John, I just want you to know, you crushed that phone call.

1230
00:48:49.260 --> 00:48:50.940
I thought you did such a good job.

1231
00:48:51.320 --> 00:48:56.980
Now, I have done films, or I have done things where someone is on the other line.

1232
00:48:57.140 --> 00:49:02.840
For example, in season nine, when Pam breaks down crying at her desk, they figured out

1233
00:49:02.840 --> 00:49:07.680
a way to wire in John Krasinski live so I could hear him in my ear.

1234
00:49:08.000 --> 00:49:14.560
So there are times when there's a really emotional scene or a scene that really requires you to

1235
00:49:14.560 --> 00:49:19.100
speak to the other actor, but, like, 90% of the time, you are just pretending someone

1236
00:49:19.100 --> 00:49:19.320
is there.

1237
00:49:19.320 --> 00:49:19.920
There's no one there.

1238
00:49:20.260 --> 00:49:20.580
Yeah.

1239
00:49:20.840 --> 00:49:21.200
Exactly.

1240
00:49:21.400 --> 00:49:25.580
And so John was just talking to Mr. Decker, who wasn't there, and I just thought he did

1241
00:49:25.580 --> 00:49:26.440
such a great job.

1242
00:49:26.620 --> 00:49:29.700
So anyway, I just had to give a little love to J.K.

1243
00:49:29.700 --> 00:49:37.520
Yeah, and after that scene, when Jim finds out that he has lost the sale, that Dwight stole

1244
00:49:37.520 --> 00:49:42.740
the sale, that is 25% of his income, he goes back into the conference room where Michael

1245
00:49:42.740 --> 00:49:48.860
is wrapping things up, and everyone is bored to tears, and that is when Pam falls asleep

1246
00:49:48.860 --> 00:49:50.080
on Jim's shoulder.

1247
00:49:51.760 --> 00:49:59.980
And we filmed that about, oh, my goodness, like, 15, 16 times, that scene, because this

1248
00:49:59.980 --> 00:50:02.480
was our Jim Pam moment of the episode.

1249
00:50:02.660 --> 00:50:03.580
This was it.

1250
00:50:03.640 --> 00:50:07.940
And they really wanted to get these little Jim Pam moments just perfectly.

1251
00:50:08.220 --> 00:50:12.980
I looked up this scene in the script, and there is a piece of stage direction that B.J.

1252
00:50:13.100 --> 00:50:17.400
Novak wrote that I want to read for you because I think it is so perfect.

1253
00:50:17.400 --> 00:50:24.840
He wrote, Jim reacts to Pam falling asleep on him like a butterfly has landed on his shoulder.

1254
00:50:25.640 --> 00:50:26.120
Aww.

1255
00:50:26.600 --> 00:50:27.780
Isn't that so poetic?

1256
00:50:27.980 --> 00:50:28.940
That's so poetic.

1257
00:50:28.940 --> 00:50:30.220
That is so sweet.

1258
00:50:30.540 --> 00:50:36.200
And so that's what John had in his mind, was that was his, you know, inspiration for how

1259
00:50:36.200 --> 00:50:37.120
to react to that.

1260
00:50:37.300 --> 00:50:38.100
That is so sweet.

1261
00:50:38.100 --> 00:50:41.980
Like, how special to have a butterfly land on your shoulder, and you don't want to move,

1262
00:50:42.060 --> 00:50:43.760
and you want to savor it.

1263
00:50:43.760 --> 00:50:44.400
Yeah, you don't want to disturb it.

1264
00:50:44.560 --> 00:50:44.720
Yeah.

1265
00:50:44.800 --> 00:50:45.120
Yeah.

1266
00:50:45.560 --> 00:50:46.860
Oh, that is so sweet.

1267
00:50:47.200 --> 00:50:51.960
Well, I wrote, you know, this is equally as just insightful, you guys.

1268
00:50:52.120 --> 00:50:58.300
I wrote on my note card, what a great jam moment at the end, and Jenna's skin looks flawless.

